        <p>Looking back, the journey started with a simple question: <em>how are programming languages created?</em></p>

        <p>I didn’t fully understand what I was signing up for when I decided to answer that question by building one. But I knew I wanted to learn, and I was willing to put in the work.</p>

        <p>From that first idea in January, through a nervous proposal defence in February, to a working interpreter in April, version 0.1 in June, and a polished project by August, TongaLang has been one of the most demanding and rewarding engineering experiences I’ve undertaken.</p>

        <p>I am proud of how far the project has come, and I’m looking forward to seeing what it can become.</p>

        <p class="story-closing">This is TongaLang. And the journey continues.</p>

        <p class="article-byline">Written by Leo Mabuku · Software developer and Computer Science graduate · <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a></p>
